    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe string membership **tier** (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) is replaced with a numeric **`membershipLevel`** (1\u20133), derived on creation:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` response property (string, `GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE`) with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, read-only). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field and drops the old one.\n\n- **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 retargeted the mapping to `membershipLevel` and rewrote the method: start at 1; +1 when an email is present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; `Math.min(level, 3)` cap. The old `householdMemberCount >= 3 \u2192 GOLD` logic is gone (level 4 is reserved for tenure, per the spec).\n\n- **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (via `ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner)`) instead of the tier.\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test `coreNumericLevel` (email present + unique name \u21d2 `membershipLevel == 3`) passes, and the audit log confirms `... membershipLevel=3`.\n\nNote: the spec said \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead.\" The existing audit line didn't actually include the tier, so I added `membershipLevel` to it to satisfy that requirement \u2014 flag me if you'd prefer it left off.",
