        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `membershipLevel(Owner)` replaces `membershipTier(Owner)` in the same place in `OwnerMapper`, sitting alongside the other sibling derivations (`membershipNumber`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`) and following their exact idiom: null guard first, then derive from owner fields. A maintainer would find it natural.\n- **No duplication of the formula.** The audit line in `OwnerRestControllerV1` calls `ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner)` rather than reinlining the computation, keeping the mapper as the single source of truth \u2014 the right call even though it means the level is computed once for the audit and once in `toOwnerDto`; that recomputation is negligible and preferable to duplicating the rule.\n- **No catch-all growth.** Nothing is being piled onto an unrelated class; the OpenAPI schema change is co-located with the field definition and matches the Javadoc/spec wording.\n- **Consistency verified.** No stray `membershipTier` references remain in source; the generated DTO, controller, and schema all line up.\n\nOne out-of-diff observation (not blocking): `Owner.householdMemberCount` is still populated in `ClinicServiceImpl` but is now read nowhere, since the old GOLD tier was its only consumer. Cleaning that up is a separate concern from this diff's structure \u2014 the field may be intentionally retained for the reserved tenure logic \u2014 so it doesn't affect the verdict."
